{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_user_stories_milestone_1_us_107_running_stitch_pattern_us_107", "label": "US-107 \u2014 Running stitch pattern", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/user-stories/milestone-1/US-107-running-stitch-pattern.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Patterns receive position and heading \u2014 not the movement vector \u2014 because zigzag and sew-up derive geometry from the needle's heading, and the two differ under goto/glide. Patterns are pure state machines returning stitch positions so the stream stays the single writer and patterns test without a stream. Two types mirror Catroid: a lifecycle wrapper (activate/pause/resume/stop) and the pattern state machine it delegates to."}, {"id": "docs_user_stories_milestone_1_us_107_running_stitch_pattern_stitchpattern_protocol", "label": "StitchPattern protocol and NeedleUpdate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/user-stories/milestone-1/US-107-running-stitch-pattern.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`mutating func update(_: NeedleUpdate) -> [StagePoint]` \u2014 amended from returning [Stitch] because Stitch carries converted embroidery units plus jump/colour flags, all of which belong to the stream rather than the pattern."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_user_stories_milestone_1_us_107_running_stitch_pattern_us_107", "target": "docs_user_stories_milestone_1_us_102_stitch_model_and_stream_us_102", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/user-stories/milestone-1/US-107-running-stitch-pattern.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_user_stories_milestone_1_us_107_running_stitch_pattern_us_107", "target": "docs_decisions_adr_007", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/user-stories/mile